[Unit]
Description=Omarchy installation
Wants=omarchy-install-cpu-boost.service
# The umbrella for the install's systemd-run phases. The orchestrator starts
# it when an install begins; phase units (and the keyring init) declare
# PartOf= it, so `systemctl stop omarchy-install.target` is a group abort
# that takes every running phase's cgroup down with it. As phases migrate
# from the orchestrator's loop into units of their own, their ordering moves
# here as After=/Requires= edges.
#
# The destruction boundary: the disk phase (still inside the orchestrator's
# install step) partitions, formats and mounts the target, and every phase
# unit here runs strictly after it. The After= chain documents that order,
# and run-phase enforces it independently — a hosted phase refuses to run
# unless the target is a mountpoint, so a stray start or a mis-edged graph
# fails loudly instead of writing into the live system.
